 {:seon.task/name "the-schema-map-is-read-once-a-value"
  :seon.task/plan "Approved by the owner, 2026-11-08, as a Datahike fork change. Found 2026-11-07 and in an audit 2026-11-08: datahike.api/schema rebuilds the whole schema map on each call, 241 k ticks against 20 for (:schema db) on the same db. seon.merge/merge-tx read it per carried datom (418 M ticks a real merge, now 24 M), and seon.task/carry-tx did once before (774 MB at 100 tasks). 14 calls remain in src. The class goes when d/schema is cheap on a db value: built once and kept with it, in Datahike, which needs the owner's go as a fork change; otherwise each caller reads (:schema db), whose shape must be checked against d/schema's (equal for every ident on main's db, checked). Proof: a cost proof that calls d/schema n times on one value and costs O(1) after the first."
