{:seon.task/name "a-small-write-costs-its-minimum"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-08: a small write (a few datoms on one entity) costs 0.3 M ticks committed, 0.11 M of it the in-memory transaction (d/with) and about 0.19 M the commit. The first-principles minimum is about 0.1 M: each datom into EAVT, AEVT and AVET by path copy (about 2 k a datom an index), about 12 rewritten nodes serialized and written (about 5 k each), the commit record, group commit with no sync. Owner, 2026-11-08: \"The point is to make this process so cheap that we can write more often.\" Profile one small write by phase (transact pipeline, schema reads, tx-meta, node serialization, the commit record) and remove what is beyond the minimum. Then each watcher of main's commits (the reconciler, the render proc) answers \"did this transaction touch what I read\" in O(ops x log reads), a few k ticks. STOP: a small write above 0.2 M; notice handling growing with main's size."
